        "affinity": 0.9126344552217013,
        "properties": {
          "description": "Beck Hansen is an American singer-songwriter and multi-instrumentalist celebrated for eclectic, genre-blending music that mixes folk, hip-hop, electronic, rock and experimental pop. Rising from the early-90s anti-folk and underground scenes in Los Angeles and New York, he broke into the mainstream with the 1994 hit \"Loser\" and consolidated critical and commercial success with albums such as Odelay, Sea Change, Morning Phase and Colors. His work is marked by inventive sampling, ironic and poetic lyrics, diverse production approaches and frequent collaborations with producers and guest musicians.",
